From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:26:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fast-shelf-scroll

Holding Left or Right on a shelf of 60 or more carts moves 3 carts per
repeat after 30 repeats (about 2 s). While it is fast the row is kept
within one cart of the selection so it never runs off the screen, no
cart face is asked for, and carts without one draw as their
label-coloured placeholder. After the hold, until the row has settled
and every visible face is back, the face loader still waits for none and
the selected ROM is not prefetched, so no frame blocks on the card. Once
that trail ends, the device logs `slot: fast scroll:` with the frame
count, p50, p99 and max frame time (the release and settle frames
included), the panel period, and the frames that showed a placeholder or
an empty row.

Adapted from marghost/slot_modded efe32cd and 0fce212, which take it from
stevolarn/slot, GPL-3.0.
